  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q94-98-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p5-q94",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sec(180^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\operatorname{cosec}(180^\\circ+\\theta)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sec(180^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\operatorname{cosec}(180^\\circ+\\theta)} &= \\frac{-\\sec\\theta}{-\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{\\sec(180^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\operatorname{cosec}(180^\\circ+\\theta)} &= \\frac{1/\\cos\\theta}{1/\\sin\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{\\sec(180^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\operatorname{cosec}(180^\\circ+\\theta)} &= \\tan\\theta\\end{align*}$$\nThe original expression requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q95",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sin(180^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\cot(180^\\circ+\\theta)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin(180^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\cot(180^\\circ+\\theta)} &= \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cot\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{\\sin(180^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\cot(180^\\circ+\\theta)} &= \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta/\\sin\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{\\sin(180^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\cot(180^\\circ+\\theta)} &= \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original expression requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q96",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sec(-\\theta)+\\operatorname{cosec}(-\\theta)}{\\tan(-\\theta)-\\cot(-\\theta)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p5-q96-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-\\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p5-q96-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use negative-angle identities, reduce to sine and cosine, then factor the difference of squares. Retain the original domain.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sec(-\\theta)+\\operatorname{cosec}(-\\theta)}{\\tan(-\\theta)-\\cot(-\\theta)} &= \\frac{\\sec\\theta-\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta}{\\cot\\theta-\\tan\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{\\sec(-\\theta)+\\operatorname{cosec}(-\\theta)}{\\tan(-\\theta)-\\cot(-\\theta)} &= \\frac{\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}}{\\dfrac{\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}} \\\\ \\frac{\\sec(-\\theta)+\\operatorname{cosec}(-\\theta)}{\\tan(-\\theta)-\\cot(-\\theta)} &= \\frac{\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{\\sec(-\\theta)+\\operatorname{cosec}(-\\theta)}{\\tan(-\\theta)-\\cot(-\\theta)} &= \\frac{\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta}{(\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta)(\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta)} \\\\ \\frac{\\sec(-\\theta)+\\operatorname{cosec}(-\\theta)}{\\tan(-\\theta)-\\cot(-\\theta)} &= -\\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original expression requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$, $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos^2\\theta\\ne\\sin^2\\theta$. These restrictions remain after cancellation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q97",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\tan(180^\\circ+\\theta)}-\\dfrac{1}{\\tan(180^\\circ-\\theta)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\cot\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\tan(180^\\circ+\\theta)}-\\frac{1}{\\tan(180^\\circ-\\theta)} &= \\frac{1}{\\tan\\theta}-\\frac{1}{-\\tan\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\tan(180^\\circ+\\theta)}-\\frac{1}{\\tan(180^\\circ-\\theta)} &= \\frac{2}{\\tan\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\tan(180^\\circ+\\theta)}-\\frac{1}{\\tan(180^\\circ-\\theta)} &= 2\\cot\\theta\\end{align*}$$\nThe original expression requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$; both tangents must be defined and nonzero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q98",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sec(180^\\circ-\\theta)}+\\dfrac{1}{\\operatorname{cosec}(180^\\circ+\\theta)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\sec(180^\\circ-\\theta)}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosec}(180^\\circ+\\theta)} &= -\\frac{1}{\\sec\\theta}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sec(180^\\circ-\\theta)}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosec}(180^\\circ+\\theta)} &= -\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sec(180^\\circ-\\theta)}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosec}(180^\\circ+\\theta)} &= -(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)\\end{align*}$$\nThe original expression requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
